The core Go module is news_panel. cmd/fusion and FUSION_* configuration names
remain compatible with upstream deployments. Plugin writes require INGEST_TOKEN
independently of the upstream reader session/password configuration.

Third-party dependencies retain their own licenses. Go module license metadata
was checked for the 47 modules in go.mod; npm license metadata was checked for
all 621 versions in pnpm-lock.yaml. No declared GPL/AGPL license was found.
This is a manifest/registry audit, not a source-level legal certification.

Notable non-MIT/BSD/Apache metadata in the upstream frontend toolchain:
- Lightning CSS and its platform build packages: MPL-2.0 (build tooling).
- DOMPurify: Apache-2.0 OR MPL-2.0; news_panel elects Apache-2.0.
- Geist, Geist Mono, Inter variable fonts: SIL Open Font License 1.1.
- caniuse-lite browser data: CC-BY-4.0.
Retain applicable package licenses and notices when redistributing dependencies.
Font licenses are copied into the SPA under /licenses/ for binary distribution.

Collected license texts for 47 Go modules and 103 production npm package entries
are provided in backend/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt and copied into the container at
/usr/share/licenses/news_panel/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt. Packages whose tarballs
omit license text use their upstream repository license (the source URL is
recorded; react-remove-scroll-bar uses upstream master because its registry
gitHead is unavailable).
